  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-61" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NEXTERA ENERGY TRANSMISSION NEW YORK, INC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;FOR THE SIX MONTHS ENDED JUNE 30, 2026 and 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;(in thousands unless otherwise noted)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;text-decoration:underline"&gt;__________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting that varies from generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America ("GAAP"). These requirements differ from GAAP related to (1) the presentation of regulatory debits and credits (2) the presentation of deferred income taxes (3) the presentation of regulatory assets and liabilities and (4) the presentation of equity carrying charges (5) the presentation of accruals associated with the cost of removal included within the accumulated depreciation reserve. Accordingly, certain footnotes are not prepared on the same basis as the financial statements presented herein.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements should be read in conjunction with the 2025 FERC Form 1 of NextEra Energy Transmission New York, Inc. ("the Company"). In the opinion of the Company's management, all adjustments considered necessary for fair financial statement presentation have been made. The results of operations for an interim period generally will not give a true indication of results for the year. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;REGULATORY MATTERS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Formula Rate Filings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;On June 28, 2024, NEET NY posted its 2023 Actual Revenue Requirement and True Up Adjustment (2024 Posting) on the New York Independent System Operator, Inc.'s website. On July 11, 2024, a group of customers requested that NEET NY provide additional information explaining the operational expenses included in NEET NY's 2024 Posting. Throughout the remainder of the year, NEET NY provided information to the customer group supporting the operational expenses. On February 13, 2025, the customer group opened an Informal Challenge (Challenge) into NEET NY 2024 Posting. Subsequent to the Challenge, NEET NY and the customer group engaged in settlement discussions. As a result of these discu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;ssions, NEET NY has booked an estimated refund of $13,695, for costs previously collected from customers. Of this amount, approximately $8,008 was moved to Other Non-Current Assets and the remainder to a non-recoverable expense account. The estimated amount owed to customers, inclusive of $1,598 of interest and over recoveries, as of December 31, 2024, is $15,661, which is recorded as a regulatory liability. As of June 30, 2026, the balance owed to customers is $8,435. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%"&gt;In addition to the amounts agreed to with customers, NEET NY wrote off $3,895 of regulatory assets related to development spend. The settlement agreement was finalized and executed in May 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;State Regulatory Proceedings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;In July 2025, the New York Public Service Commission withdrew the New York City Offshore Wind Public Policy Transmission Need, which resulted in the Company writing off approximately $10,170, which is inclusive of the $8,008 referenced above.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;ELECTRIC UTILITY PLANT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Electric utility plant consists of the following as of:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:92.708%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:50.103%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:22.656%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.923%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:22.818%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;June 30, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000;padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:12pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" st